From d7986d934bcdfeef091f2b5848375f52a524483d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corpus review <review@local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:37:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Add thin leader-line pointers across chapters and
 de-clutter dense plates

- part-pins.js: new pointer pass for parts that only had a written note.
  274 parts gain the same dot + hairline leader + name label that the rest of
  the atlas uses (heart, brain, spleen, liver, gut, pancreas, thyroid, bladder,
  uterus/cervix/vagina/support, male pelvis+testis+prostate, clitoral complex,
  penile erectile tissue, facial and trigeminal nerves, eye, retina, nephron,
  brachial plexus, deep cerebrum, meninges/CSF, brainstem, pulmonary acinus,
  hepatic lobule, intestinal wall, skin layers, labor stages 1-2, placenta,
  fetal development, anatomical language, body regions).
- 11 tissue-level rows (alveoli, glomerulus/tubules, lobule, villi, islets,
  acini, follicle) point at their existing microscope cutaways instead of a
  false pin on a gross plate.
- app.js: declutterLabels() hides labels that would print over another label
  (dot + leader stay, name stays in the Structure labels list), so no chapter
  shows stacked text. Verified 0 overlaps across all 74 chapters.
- index.html: cache-bust to v=49.
